I'll read the review brief first, then the full motion bundle, and rule only on the front-end / three.js questions you listed.{"lens":"Front-end and three.js implementation","verdict":"changes_requested","summary":"CSS3D must WRAP the existing tile DOM as an opt-in mode, not replace it; fix tension-4 blur myth, specify layout→matrix3d handoff, gesture/focus rules, and a tree-shaken import cap.","tension_rulings":[{"tension":4,"ruling":"change","why":"Choose CSS3DRenderer for DOM/a11y preservation; drop the blur claim—real costs are ~68 composited layers, matrix3d layout ownership, and gesture conflicts, not inherent text blur."},{"tension":6,"ruling":"change","why":"Trade is only defensible if three.js is progressive enhancement on the 22.5 KB 2D file with a tree-shaken CSS3D+camera surface (~100–115 KB gzip) and a hard kill-switch when budget or reduced-motion forbids it."}],"findings":[{"id":"F1","severity":"high","section":"Part 3 tension 4 / Part 2 Proposed technique","problem":"The brief still says CSS3D 'blurs text under transforms', contradicting Part 1's correction; implementers will re-litigate the wrong criterion and may abandon DOM for WebGL unnecessarily.","instruction":"Rewrite tension 4 criteria as: (1) DOM preservation and existing accessible names/focus, (2) compositing cost of ~68 permanent CSS3D layers on mobile GPUs, (3) loss of CSS grid/flex as layout engine under matrix3d, (4) WebGL only if dual-rendering a11y content—which this budget and single-file constraint forbid. Decision: CSS3DRenderer; WebGL text quads are out.","basis":"principle"},{"id":"F2","severity":"high","section":"Part 1 hard constraint 3; Part 2 Proposed technique","problem":"Brief never states whether three.js replaces, wraps, or coexists with the working 2D DOM; dual trees would duplicate names, search targets, and dialogs and break a11y.","instruction":"Pick WRAP-as-mode: one tile element per mechanism remains the sole accessible content. Entering 3D mode: detach tiles from the packed grid container, wrap each in CSS3DObject (same Element reference), parent into the CSS3D scene. Exiting 3D / prefers-reduced-motion / failed load: re-parent those exact nodes back into the 2D packed layout and tear down the renderer. Search, filters, dialog, focusables, and accessible names never clone; protocol dim/number state stays on the same nodes via existing classes/ARIA. three.js runs alongside as a view mode, never as a second content source.","basis":"principle"},{"id":"F3","severity":"medium","section":"Part 1 payload; Part 3 tension 6","problem":"Budget headroom is ~127 KB gzip; an unscoped three import will blow the 150 KB cap or leave no room for mode glue.","instruction":"Minimum import surface: `Scene`, `PerspectiveCamera`, `Object3D`/`Math` used by CSS3D (`Vector3`, `Quaternion`, `Matrix4`, `Euler` as pulled), plus `examples/jsm/renderers/CSS3DRenderer` (`CSS3DRenderer`, `CSS3DObject`). No WebGLRenderer, no full OrbitControls trackball, no loaders/geometries/materials/fonts. Constrain camera with a ~30-line dolly+yaw helper. Target ~100–115 KB gzip for that surface; measure post-bundle and fail CI if total page >150 KB gzip. Defensible only as progressive enhancement over the canonical 2D file—not if 3D becomes required for any feature.","basis":"principle"},{"id":"F4","severity":"high","section":"Part 1 prior cut grounds; Part 2 camera; Part 3 tension 4","problem":"Camera drag and ~68 clickable/focusable tiles conflict; a focused tile can sit behind another in Z and become unreachable without a defined strategy.","instruction":"Pointer: primary button down records clientX/Y; if movement ≤6px and duration <300ms → click the topmost tile under point (elementFromPoint on the DOM tile); if >6px → camera dolly/small-orbit only, suppress click. No free trackball; max yaw/pitch such that tiles stay within ~10° of face-on. Focus: camera-follows-focus—on focusin of a tile, animate camera target/dolly so that tile is centered, face-on, and unoccluded; temporarily raise that CSS3DObject's z (or sort order) while focused, restore on blur. Never focus-follows-camera (roving focus on drift would be hostile). Keyboard: Tab order remains document order of the same DOM tiles; parallax drift pauses while focus is inside the table.","basis":"principle"},{"id":"F5","severity":"high","section":"Part 1 packed layout; Part 2 CSS3D proposal","problem":"Packed layout is CSS grid + wrapping flex blocks; CSS3D positions via matrix3d and cannot inherit grid packing—without an explicit geometry pipeline, tiles will stack or desync on resize.","instruction":"Own layout in JS for both modes from one pure function: input = filtered element list + container width + tile min size + gap + family-run rules; output = Map<id,{x,y,width,height,depthRow}>. 2D mode applies those boxes via absolute positioning or grid-template placement generated from the map. 3D mode sets each CSS3DObject.position to (x - originX, originY - y, zOf(depthRow)) with z stepping by a fixed plane gap (e.g. depth index × constant), scale 1, rotation (0,0,0). On resize (ResizeObserver, debounced one rAF): recompute map; 2D reapplies boxes; 3D writes new positions (snap if reduced-motion, short tween otherwise). Never leave tiles as CSS grid children while parented under CSS3DRenderer.","basis":"principle"},{"id":"F6","severity":"medium","section":"Part 2 proposed motion; production risk","problem":"Three failure modes will make the product feel broken: mobile compositor thrash with ~68 layers; click/orbit misfires; layout/scene desync after filter or resize.","instruction":"Ship gates: (1) profile 68 CSS3D layers on a mid-tier mobile—if sustained jank, auto-fallback to 2D; (2) enforce the 6px pointer threshold and click suppression; (3) single layout function as sole position source. Refuse to ship without the WRAP + re-parent path that keeps one focusable DOM tile set fully keyboard-navigable in both modes (including unocclusion-on-focus). Decorative assembly/parallax may degrade; the dual-tree or WebGL-only tile path may not.","basis":"principle"}],"what_to_keep":"Constrained camera (no free trackball, tiles parallel to the view plane) plus CSS3D so tiles remain real DOM with existing accessible names.","dissent_note":"Pedagogy and visual-design lenses may reject Z-depth and payload as decorative; this lens still requires the wrap-mode and focus contracts if three.js ships."}
